      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 3 A Trip to Bhopal Notes\nChapter 4 TickTickTick\nThis is among the most important chapters as you will be learning how to tell time using analogue clocks. As you are trying to understand how to tell time, it will help you become punctual.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnderstanding Time:\nThe chapter begins by familiarizing students with the concept of time and its importance in our daily lives.\nIntroduction to the Clock:\nIt introduces students to the analogue clock as a tool for measuring time.\nParts of a Clock:\nThe chapter explains the different parts of an analogue clock: the hour hand, the minute hand, and the second hand.\nReading the Hour Hand:\nStudents learn how the hour hand tells us the hour (e.g., 1 o'clock, 2 o'clock).\nReading the Minute Hand:\nThey are introduced to the concept of minutes and how the minute hand tells us the number of minutes past the hour (e.g., 5 minutes past 7, 10 minutes past 8).\nTelling Time:\nThe chapter combines the understanding of the hour and minute hands to tell the complete time (e.g., 7:02, 8:10).\nActivities:\nThe chapter includes exercises and activities to help students practice reading time on an analogue clock.\nChapter 4 Tick-Tick-Tick Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 4 Tick-Tick-Tick\n20 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 4 Tick-Tick-Tick\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 4 Tick-Tick-Tick",
