      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 11 Tables and Shares Notes\nChapter 12 How Heavy? How Light?\nIn this chapter, you will be learning about weight measurement along with the different units for doing the same. Through the questions, you will know weights are used in daily life and how you can match up a given weight through different loads.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnderstanding Weight:\nThe chapter explains that weight refers to how heavy or light an object is. Different objects have different weights.\nUnits of Weight:\nIt introduces common units used to measure weight, like grams (g) for lighter objects and kilograms (kg) for heavier ones. Milligrams (mg) might also be mentioned for very light objects.\nUsing a Balance:\nThe chapter emphasizes the use of a weighing balance as a tool to compare the weights of two objects. Students learn to identify which object is heavier by observing which side tilts down on the balance.\nComparing Weights:\nActivities and exercises involve comparing the weights of different objects and arranging them in order from lightest to heaviest. Students may even estimate the weight of an object before using the balance to verify.\nReal-life Applications:\nThe chapter might include relatable examples like comparing the weight of fruits, books, or school bags.\nChapter 12 How Heavy? How Light? Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 12 How Heavy? How Light?\n17 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 12 How Heavy? How Light?\nS.No.\nImportant Links For Chapter 12 How Heavy? How Light?",
