      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 13 Fields and Fences Notes\nChapter 14 Smart Charts\nThis chapter involved pictorial representation of information. With pie charts and pictographs, you will learn how to handle information. It will also help you develop an intuition for numbers.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nIntroduction to Data:\nStudents learn what data is and how it's collected in everyday situations.\nTables:\nThe chapter explains how data can be organized in rows and columns using tables for better understanding.\nConcept of Charts:\nIt introduces students to the concept of charts as a visual representation of data.\nTypes of Charts:\nThe chapter focuses on two main types of charts commonly used at this level:\nBar Charts:\nThese charts use bars of different heights to represent data points, making it easy to compare quantities.\nPie Charts:\nPie charts are circular charts divided into slices, where each slice represents a portion of the whole data.\nInterpreting Charts:\nStudents learn how to read and interpret information presented in charts. This includes understanding the labels, titles, and how the data is visually represented.\nReal-life Applications:\nThe chapter uses relatable examples like favourite TV shows, food preferences, and playtime to demonstrate how charts can be used in everyday situations.\nChapter 14 Smart Charts Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 14 Smart Charts\n17 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 14 Smart Charts\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 14 Smart Charts",
