      "q": "1.\nChapter 5 The Way the World Looks Notes\nChapter 6 The Junk Seller\nIn this chapter, you will be introduced to the concept of selling and buying. Through a story, this chapter will help you understand how earning, loan, sales, and expenditure works so that you are able to function in the real world better.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnderstanding the Concept of a Junk Seller:\nThe chapter begins by explaining who a junk seller is and what they collect.\nIntroduction to Multiplication:\nThrough Kiran's work of collecting and selling various items like plastic, newspaper, iron, and brass, the chapter introduces multiplication as a concept.\nMultiplying a Number by Itself:\nKiran collects multiple kilograms of each material. The chapter uses this scenario to introduce multiplying a number by itself.\nFinding the Total Cost:\nThe chapter presents word problems where Kiran has to calculate the total cost based on the weight of the material and the price per kilogram. This involves multiplying the weight by the price per kilogram.\nEstimating the Total Cost:\nThe chapter also touches upon estimation. By rounding off the weight to a nearby tens place, students can estimate the total cost before performing the actual multiplication.\nChapter 6 The Junk Seller Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 6 The Junk Seller\n13 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 6 The Junk Seller\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 6 The Junk Seller",
