      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 6 The Junk Seller Notes\nChapter 7 Jugs and Mugs\nThis chapter is all about measuring liquids. You will start by measuring water in large units like litres and then move on to some smaller units like millilitres. You will also learn how to convert one unit into another.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnits of Capacity:\nThe chapter introduces litres (L) and millilitres (mL) as units to measure the amount of liquid a container can hold.\nEstimating Capacity:\nStudents learn to estimate how much liquid a container can hold by comparing it to familiar objects like mugs or bottles.\nMeasuring Capacity:\nThe chapter explains how to use measuring containers like jugs and mugs to measure liquids accurately in litres and millilitres.\nAdding and Subtracting Capacity:\nStudents practice adding and subtracting the capacities of different containers.\nWord Problems:\nThe chapter includes word problems that involve applying concepts of capacity to real-life situations.\nChapter 7 Jugs and Mugs Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 7 Jugs and Mugs\n17 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 7 Jugs and Mugs\nS.No\nImportant Links for Chapter 7 Jugs and Mugs",
