      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 10 Play with Patterns Notes\nChapter 11 Tables and Shares\nThis chapter is all about how division is applicable in everyday life. You will learn how to divide an object into groups and rows.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnderstanding Multiplication through Arrangements:\nThe chapter starts by showing how multiplication relates to arranging objects in rows and columns. Students see how the total number of objects can be calculated by finding the product of the number of rows and the number of objects in each row.\nIntroduction to Tables:\nThe chapter emphasizes the importance of memorizing multiplication tables from 1 to 10. These tables help with quick calculations and solving problems.\nConcept of Sharing:\nThe chapter explains division as the concept of sharing a total quantity into equal parts. Students solve problems where they need to divide a given number of objects among a certain number of people or groups.\nRelating Multiplication and Division:\nThe chapter highlights the connection between multiplication and division. It shows that multiplication is the opposite of division.\nChapter 11 Tables and Shares Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 11 Tables and Shares\n27 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 11 Tables and Shares\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 11 Tables and Shares",
