      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 12 How Heavy? How Light? Notes\nChapter 13 Fields and Fences\nIn this chapter, you will be learning about perimeter and area through things like fields and fences.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnderstanding Fences and Fields:\nThe chapter introduces the concept of fields, which are areas of land used for growing crops or plants. It explains how fences are used to enclose these fields and separate them from other areas.\nPerimeter and Boundary:\nThe chapter introduces the concept of perimeter as the total length of the boundary surrounding a closed figure. It explains that to find the total length of the fence needed for a field, we need to find the perimeter of the field.\nCalculating Perimeter of Shapes:\nThe chapter focuses on calculating the perimeter of simple shapes like squares and rectangles. It teaches students how to add the lengths of all the sides of a shape to find its total perimeter.\nWord Problems:\nThe chapter includes engaging word problems where students apply their understanding of perimeter to real-life scenarios. For instance, they might be asked to calculate the amount of wire needed to fence a rectangular field or the distance covered by someone walking around a field.\nRelating Perimeter to Area:\nWhile the chapter mainly focuses on perimeter, it might also briefly touch upon the concept of area. Students might be introduced to the idea that a bigger perimeter often indicates a larger area, although not always.\nChapter 13 Fields and Fences Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 13 Fields and Fences\nQuestion & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 13 Fields and Fences\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 13 Fields and Fences",
