      "q": "2.\nClass 4 Chapter 8 Carts and Wheels Notes\nChapter 9 Halves and Quarters\nFraction is one of the most important concepts that you will be studying. Up until now, you have mostly been dealing with whole numbers. This chapter will gradually introduce the concept to you where you will learn about quarters, halves, and wholes.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nIntroduction to Halves\n: The chapter introduces the idea of dividing something whole into two equal parts. It uses relatable examples like sharing a chapati between two friends.\nRepresenting Halves\n: The concept of half is symbolically represented by the fraction 1/2.\nDividing Halves Further\n: The chapter explains how one half can be further divided into two equal parts, resulting in fourths or quarters.\nRepresenting Quarters\n: A quarter is symbolised by the fraction 1/4.\nRelating Halves and Quarters\n: The chapter explores the connection between halves and quarters. For instance, two quarters together make one whole, and half of a whole can be further divided into two quarters.\nChapter 9 Halves and Quarters Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 9 Halves and Quarters\n28 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 9 Halves and Quarters\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 9 Halves and Quarters",
