      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 7 Jugs and Mugs Notes\nChapter 8 Carts and Wheels\nOne of the most interesting geometric shapes to study is circles. However, since they don\u2019t have any proper fixed-length sides, you can master them easily. This chapter will introduce you to the concept of circle and radius along with its circumference.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nIntroduction to Circles:\nRecognizing everyday objects that are round or circular in shape.\nMaking Circles:\nUsing simple objects like bangles or coins to trace circles on paper or ground.\nProperties of Circles:\nIntroduction to the concept of radius as the distance from the centre of the circle to any point on the edge.\nActivities with Circles:\nComparing the sizes of circles made with different objects. Relating circles to games and rhymes children play.\nChapter 8 Carts and Wheels Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 8 Carts and Wheels\n17 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 8 Carts and Wheels\nS.No\nImportant Links for Chapter 8 Carts and Wheels",
