      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 1 Building with Bricks Notes\nChapter 2 Long and Short\nIn this chapter, you will be learning how to deal with lengths. This covers measurements in meters and centimetres and conversion between the same. You will learn how to solve these questions in an easy way.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nUnderstanding Long and Short:\nThis section introduces the basic idea of comparing the lengths of two objects. It helps students differentiate between longer and shorter objects.\nUsing Measuring Tools:\nThe chapter emphasizes the importance of using tools like a ruler to measure lengths accurately.\nComparing Objects:\nStudents will practice comparing the lengths of various objects in everyday situations. This can involve activities like comparing pencils, crayons, or even their own footsteps.\nOrdering Objects:\nThe chapter progresses to ordering three or more objects based on their lengths. Students will arrange objects from shortest to longest (or vice versa).\nChapter 2 Long and Short Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 2 Long and Short\n20 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 2 Long and Short\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 2 Long and Short",
