      "q": "1.\nClass 4 Chapter 2 Long and Short Notes\nChapter 3 A Trip to Bhopal\nThis has to be one of the most interesting chapters. Through a short adventure in the city of Bhopal, you will be introduced to the important concept of mathematics.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nAddition:\nCalculating the total number of students going on the Trip by adding the number of students from each class (grade level)\nMultiplication:\nDetermining the total number of oranges, bananas, and biscuits needed for the Trip by multiplying the number of students by the quantity given to each student\nDivision:\nFiguring out how many buses are required to transport all the students if each bus has a specific seating capacity (This might involve finding a common divisor)\nUnderstanding Place Value:\nIdentifying a number within a given range (e.g., finding a number between 100 and 150)\nProblem-solving:\nUsing critical thinking to choose a boat for a Trip based on factors like the number of people, ticket prices, and desired Trip duration\nChapter 3 A Trip to Bhopal Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 3 A Trip to Bhopal\n17 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 3 A Trip to Bhopal\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 3 A Trip to Bhopal",
