      "q": "2.\nClass 4 Chapter 4 Tick-Tick-Tick Notes\nChapter 5 The Way The World Looks\nThis chapter is focused on perspectives and dimensions of the real world. This includes different viewing profiles of a chapter and differences between 2D and 3D objects.\nHere's a breakdown of the topics covered in this chapter:\nSeeing Things from Different Directions:\nThe chapter introduces the idea that objects can be viewed from various angles, such as the front, back, top, bottom, and sides.\nUnderstanding Relative Positions:\nIt helps students understand that directions like left, right, front, and back can change depending on your own position relative to the object.\nRepresenting 3D Shapes in 2D:\nThe chapter introduces students to the concept of drawing 2D representations (like front view, top view, side view) of 3D shapes like buildings and objects.\nChapter 5 The Way the World Looks Questions and Solutions in PDF Format\nChapter 5 The Way The World Looks\n8 Question & Solutions\nOther Related Links for Class 4 Maths Chapter 5 The Way The World Looks\nS.No.\nImportant Links for Chapter 5 The Way the World Looks",
      "a": "Detailed solution available."
